NOTE:

streamfunction8 is for navier_stokes[8-9]

The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

navier_stokes1 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Steady flow, gradual increase of the Reynolds number.
 Physical quantities.

navier_stokes2 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a 3D cavity. Two moving boundaries,
 and Re=500. Either Picard or Newton or a combination of both can be used for
 the iteration process

navier_stokes3 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Steady flow, gradual increase of the Reynolds number.
 The Stokes system matrix is saved, for increased performance
 Physical quantities.

navier_stokes4 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Crank-Nicolson time discretization

navier_stokes5 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.

navier_stokes6 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Crank-Nicolson time discretization with a predictor for the convection
 velocity at tn+1 based on extrapolation from two previous time steps:
   u_hat=2*un-un-1
 First time step: predictor is un.

navier_stokes7 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Semi-implicit Crank-Nicolson/Adams-Bashforth time discretization
 First time step: replace AB2 with explicit Euler.
 Keep LU decomposition for later time steps to reduce CPU time.

navier_stokes8 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Weak constraint on the particle domain.
 Neutrally buoyant particle ( density of particle = density of fluid )

navier_stokes9 

 Navier-Stokes problem on gravitational sedimentation of a particle in a
 rectangular box.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.
 One freely moving and rotating object. Time-stepping.
 Weak constraint on the particle domain.

navier_stokes10 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Semi-implicit Crank-Nicolson/Adams-Bashforth time discretization
 Do a real semi-implicit Euler at the first step.
 Keep LU decomposition for later time steps to reduce CPU time.

 Similar to navier_stokes7, but now:
 Do a real semi-implicit Euler at the first step.

navier_stokes11 

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Semi-implicit Gear/Karniadakis time discretization
 A semi-implicit Euler at the first step.
 Keep LU decomposition for later time steps to reduce CPU time.

 Similar to navier_stokes7, but now:
 Semi-implicit Gear/Karniadakis time discretization
 A semi-implicit Euler at the first step.

navier_stokes12

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Steady flow, gradual increase of the Reynolds number.
 Physical quantities.

 Similar to navier-stokes1, but now:
 Iterative solver with block preconditioning (using pressure
 convection-diffusion).

navier_stokes13

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Semi-implicit Crank-Nicolson/Adams-Bashforth time discretization
 First time step: replace AB2 with explicit Euler.
 Keep LU decomposition for later time steps to reduce CPU time.

 Similar to navier-stokes7, but now:
 Iterative solver with block preconditioning (using pressure mass and
 diffusion matrix). M_1^{-1}+M_2^{-1} form for approximate inverse
 Schur complement.

navier_stokes14

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Semi-implicit Gear/Karniadakis time discretization
 A semi-implicit Euler at the first step.
 Keep LU decomposition for later time steps to reduce CPU time.

 Similar to navier-stokes11, but now:
 Iterative solver with block preconditioning (using pressure mass and
 diffusion matrix). M_1^{-1}+M_2^{-1} form for approximate inverse
 Schur complement.

navier_stokes15

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with Dirichlet boundary conditions.
 Unsteady flow. Compared to exact (manufactured) solution.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.
 Spectral elements.
 This problem is similar to navier_stokes5, but now with spectral elements.

navier_stokes16

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with 3D velocities.
 Steady flow, gradual increase of the Reynolds number.
 Lid-driven cavity flow in (x,y).
 Imposed flow rate in z-direction.

navier_stokes17

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with 3D velocities (curved channel).
 Steady flow, gradual increase of the Reynolds number.
 Imposed flow rate in theta-direction. Axisymmetric.

navier_stokes18

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity 3D velocities (curved channel).
 Unsteady flow. 
 Crank-Nicolson time discretization
 Imposed flow rate in theta-direction. Axisymmetric.

navier_stokes19

 Navier-Stokes problem on a square cavity with 3D velocities (curved channel).
 Unsteady flow. 
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.

